          "title": "You'll want to know: repostar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "repostar — \"to refuel, to fill up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tenemos que repostar antes de salir. We have to fill up before we leave."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A Spain word; in Latin America people say cargar gasolina or echar gasolina."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "repostar is usually traced to reposte \"store-room, larder\", from Latin repositum \"something put away\", built on pōnere \"to put\"; it first meant taking on fresh supplies."
            }
          ]
        },
